// A function from a module's `import` block must be called with its module name, including
// inside the module that declares the import.
//
// The bare name does not resolve to the import. It used to compile clean and leave an extra
// value on the stack, so an `if` consumed that instead of the result and always took the
// true branch: in unicode.qd, `c is_digit if { ... }` made digit_value answer 17 for 'A'
// rather than -1. Every module in the corpus already writes the qualified form, which is why
// nothing caught it.
//
// badimport_mod.qd calls its own imported `upper` as a bare `upper`.
use badimport_mod.qd

fn main() {
	"hi" badimport_mod::shout print nl
}
